WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.834 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-How are you?

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm terrific.
-I'm so happy to have you here

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:05.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I had a power breakfast
this morning --

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:06.172 size:84% position:42% line:92%
oatmeal and sardines --

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I've been just going
all day long.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.076
-That's so smart.
A good way to pace out your day.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know,
you need your omegas.

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You need your omegas.
-Any way you can get them.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It shows.
-Right? I'm glowing.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When I saw you backstage,
I knew that

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:19.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
there were more omegas
than normal.

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.588 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you. Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, this -- For those who
haven't seen "Pose,"

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
it takes place in the
'80s and '90s in New York.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:30.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-The LGBT ballroom scene.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you play a nurse who i
dealing with people

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:34.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
who have --
Through the AIDS crisis.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:35.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, that's right.
That's right.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:38.772
-How did you get -- How did yo
find your way into this role

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:42.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I was actually on
a flight from LAX to Kennedy

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:45.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I ran into Judith Light,
who's a friend of mine.

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:46.212 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And she was sitting
in business,

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:50.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was back in coach,
'cause I never pay for mysel

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:53.820
to fly business, unless,
you know, a gig is paying.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. You'll fly business.
-Oh, gladly. Yeah.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:01.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, on the way out, I ran into
her and Steven Canals,

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's one of the creators,
and Our Lady J,

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:08.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
who is a fabulous trans writer
and actor and musician,

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.335 line:92%
who works on "Pose," as well

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:12.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, we were on
the escalator going down.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:15.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, JFK has
two sets of escalators.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was schmoozing with
them and having --

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:17.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
also afraid I was going to

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:21.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
fall down the escalator,
but that's a sidebar.

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:21.714 size:81% position:41% line:92%
They didn't know that.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:25.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, by the time we got to
baggage claim, I said,

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:26.119 line:92%
"What have I got to lose?"

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:28.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Hey, listen,
you know, if there's anythin

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
that works for me in terms o
a character, think of me.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I'd love to do
something on 'Pose.'"

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
A week later,
I got cast as Nurse Judy.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:39.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it just goes to show you,
if you hang out at

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:39.866 size:75% position:38% line:92%
the baggage claim --

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. That's where a lot
of people find their next job.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:48.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were living in
New York at that time.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:51.211 size:88% position:44%
-Yes. Living and doing
my first one-woman show,

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:54.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Without You I'm Nothing,"
at the Orpheum Theatre

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:54.914 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
for six months.

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:57.517 size:88% position:44%
-Which must have been an
incredibly exciting time

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:58.251 size:84% position:42% line:92%
to be in New York City.

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:00.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Everybody came to the show.
I mean, it was amazing.

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:04.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, from --
I mean, John Kennedy came,

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:05.692 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
John Kennedy Jr.

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:07.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, which, I mean,
tragically,

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.194 line:92%
he's not with us anymore.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:12.599
But people of that caliber and
then just great downtown artists

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:13.633 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and groovy people.

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:16.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
the AIDS crisis was sort o

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:18.004 line:92%
ramping up during that time.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:20.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
there was so much synergy

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:21.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so much creativity
in the city,

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause you could
still live here then.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:25.211
You know, it wasn't all built up
like, you know,

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:29.015
Hudson Yards and all these crazy
$20 million condos.

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:31.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, yeah, I just bought a
place for $10 million.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:35.622 line:92%
You know, 869 square feet.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:38.224
So, you know, there was
a lot of stuff happening.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, then, like 30 years later,
you know,

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be cast in this role
and be with these

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:45.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
incredible trans
actors and actresses

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:46.699 line:92%
who are just so talented -

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:51.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mj Rodriguez and Indya Moore
and the whole cast.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
'cause back in those days,

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:54.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, everybody who wa
trans was marginalized.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:57.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
They would never in a millio
years have been cast

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.812 line:92%
in a mainstream television show.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I try to, like, you know,
let the kids in on

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:03.950 size:81% position:41% line:92%
what it was like then.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
They just look at me and go,
"You're boring me."

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Does it -- I mean,
it must be

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:11.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
looking at the art scene now
and what it feels like

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:14.227
to be an artist in New York,
because it was all word of mouth

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
then, obviously,
before social media.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:17.263
Like, even the people that found
their way to your show,

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:19.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
it must have just been tha
they heard it was

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:20.867 size:75% position:38% line:92%
a show worth seeing.

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:22.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
you'd read the newspapers.

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:23.903 line:92%
You know, it was kind of the -

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:27.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, "Rolling Stone"
and all the great, you know,

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:29.542 size:88% position:44% line:92%
free papers of the time.

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Village Voice."
-Yeah.

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:33.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, you know,
you just picked up the phone

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:34.747 line:92%
and called people back then,

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was such a great,
you know, concept.

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:37.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You've been in New York
for a long time.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.852
Are you one of those New Yorkers
now who have had

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
the same neighbors
for a long time?

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:42.255 line:92%
Do you know your neighbors well?

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:45.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I think of myself
sort of the mayor of Chelsea

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:46.693 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay, yeah.

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:49.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Matter of fact, I just called
in a 311 emergency

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
because there's a building o
the end of the street

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:53.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
where they were
doing some reconstruction,

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:54.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
but people were bringing
their garbage,

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I called 311
and said it's a health hazard.

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:59.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, there's rodents.
There's flies.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they came
and they cleaned it up.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:03.009 line:92%
I was very proud of myself

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:04.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do they know you when
you call 311?

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:05.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are they like, "Hi, Sandra"?
-No, no, no.

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
They say, "Would you like to
remain anonymous?"

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:09.949 line:92%
I said, "No, but I'm going to.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:12.919
I said, "Nothing would make me
happier than for you to know

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:16.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Sandra Bernhard is trying
to clean up this city."

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:17.890 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:22.195
Where Bill de Blasio won't
I thought I would step in.

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:22.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Sidebar.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, anyway,
so, I have this neighbor -

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:26.199 line:92%
you know, she's wonderful.

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:30.003
Her name is Renee, and she lives
in a government-funded building,

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is in
the middle of all these

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.839 line:92%
great brownstones on my street

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:34.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
And every time
I walk past her, she goes,

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:39.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, Sandy, when you gonna be
on TV again?"

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, she's asked me
like three times a day,

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:43.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I have to, like,
kind of give her my rundown.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:46.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, then they did a really nic
profile on me recently

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:47.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
in "The New Yorker"
about "Pose."

00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:50.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, we went to visit this
you know, place,

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:53.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they interviewed Renee
a little bit.

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:54.527 line:92%
So, I ran into Renee last week

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:58.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
She goes, "Hey, Sandy,
did you see the nice piece

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:01.034 size:88% position:44% line:92%
on me in that magazine?"

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:02.135 line:92%
And then, as an afterthought

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause then she thought
maybe I'd feel bad,

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:07.307
she goes, "When are you going to
be on TV again?"

00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:10.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said,
"Thanks for nothing, Renee."

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do people come up to you
in the street,

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:13.646 size:78% position:39%
especially if you're
the mayor of Chelsea?

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:14.714 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Do you get approached?

00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:16.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, in a very nice,
casual way.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:19.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, the other day,
I was walking my dog, George

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:20.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
We all have dogs
in New York City.

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:24.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
My rescue.
And I was turning on my block.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:25.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
And every time
I cross the street,

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:28.695
if somebody's making a left,
I'll stop and hold out my hand

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:31.164
because, you know, people in
New York don't always stop

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:32.198 line:92%
for you when you have your dog

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:33.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so,
the guy turned the corner.

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:35.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
He slowed down. I got nervous.
I thought, "Oh, God.

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:37.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want to have some sort
of, like, you know,

00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:38.738 size:84% position:42% line:92%
dust-up with somebody."

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:40.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he was
a very, very cool guy.

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:40.740 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He rolled down.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes, "Honey,
I would never run you over

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:46.946 size:88% position:44%
What's happening, Sandy?
You're a great actress."

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:49.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "It's just my dog
I was worried about.

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:50.483 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank you, baby."

00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:52.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was just, like,
this great New York moment

00:05:52.452 --> 00:05:54.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
-New York City. There it is.
-You know.

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:56.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Best city in the world.
-The best.

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:59.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, and one of the reason
it's the best

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:00.793 line:92%
is someone like you being here

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:03.062
And thank you so much for making
time for us tonight.

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:05.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
What a delight.
-I'm so glad to be here.

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:06.899 line:92%
-Sandra Bernhard, everybody.

